ric category noun lacking site, etiologic, eponymic, or acronymic qualifiers, even within prepositional or clausal frames like \"history of\" or \"associated with\" that elsewhere host specific diseases. I'm carving out exceptions: qualified specific disease names fall under Modifier/SpecificDisease instead, prenominal attributive uses of generic nouns need manual flagging rather than auto-labeling, and spans inside a CompositeMention follow that rule's boundary logic. The converse clarifies that Modifier labeling requires a qualified specific disease name functioning as an attributive or history qualifier—merely appearing in a prepositional frame never justifies it on its own.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Principle: Lexical specificity, not syntactic frame, determines disease-span type.**\n  - **IF** a disease span's head is an unqualified generic category noun (a superordinate term that names a class of conditions rather than one named condition) and the span has no anatomical-site, etiologic, eponymic, or acronymic qualifier,\n  - **THEN** label it `DiseaseClass`, even when it appears in a prepositional or clausal frame that elsewhere hosts specific diseases (e.g., \"history of ___,\" \"associated with ___,\" \"characterized by ___\").\n  - **Negative constraint (does NOT apply when):**\n    - The span is itself a qualified, specific disease name (site-, eponym-, or acronym-qualified). Type it by the SpecificDisease/Modifier criteria instead.\n    - The generic noun is used prenominally as an attributive modifier of a following noun (e.g., \"___ cases\"). The available evidence does not resolve this configuration, so flag it for manual verification rather than auto-labeling it.\n    - The span is a constituent of a CompositeMention. Apply the CompositeMention boundary rules instead.\n  - **Converse safeguard:** Assign `Modifier` only to a qualified, specific disease name functioning as an attributive or history/context qualifier. A governing prepositional frame alone never justifies `Modifier`.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 1663, "output_tokens": 3002, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2550}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}